1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,080
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:35,260
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,917
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,117
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real.

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,477
Through it all, through
all the trouble and times.

20
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,077
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:28,217
So come aboard and bring along.

24
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,560
All your hopes and dreams.

25
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,877
Together we will find everything.

26
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:35,960
That we're looking for.

27
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you.

28
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,400
If you wanna be my friend.

29
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,860
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

31
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,777
You're going to be king
of the pirates right?

32
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,197
you must be completely
out of your rubbery mind.

33
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,197
Do you have any idea what that means?

34
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:01,137
yeah when he first told me it was shocking

35
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:03,497
but he's Completely
serious that's how he is.

36
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,410
i suppose.

37
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:10,757
Here's what i promised you there's three i

38
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,537
couldn't tell which was
yours so i just took

39
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:15,637
all Of them all of them belong to me i use

40
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:18,957
sentoryu the three swords
style just know that if

41
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,577
you Fight with me now
you'll be a government

42
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:23,117
defying villain so it's
either that or you're

43
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,877
left out here And killed by the Marines

44
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:28,297
execution style what are
you the son of the devil?

45
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,017
it doesn't matter Because
if I don't choose your side

46
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:34,500
I'll just end up dead on
these sticks so let's do it.

47
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:40,257
So you're finally gonna join my
crew this is the best thing ever.

48
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:43,737
You quit celebrating already
and get these ropes off me?

49
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:45,617
what the what is he?

50
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,759
Bullets just bounced right off him!

51
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,837
Straw Hat's no ordinary
human like the rest of us.

52
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,677
He must have eaten one
of those devil fruits

53
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,637
that we've heard all those rumors about.

54
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,550
Devil Fruit?

55
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:57,304
The hidden treasure of the sea!

56
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:58,342
Come on, hurry!

57
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:01,360
They got these things on here tight!

58
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,017
Come on, quit screwing around!

59
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:07,297
It doesn't matter what abilities they
have, all who oppose me are executed!

60
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:09,780
If the guns won't work, we jump! Up!

61
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:16,757
That's funny, the nuts got
tighter instead of looser.

62
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,840
Give me one of my damn swords now!

63
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,400
Luffy, look!

64
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,580
Roronoa Zoro!

65
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,320
Oh wow, that's so cool!

66
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:39,940
Make one move and you die.

67
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,880
He's scary!

68
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:49,057
Today I officially become a
criminal, having fought the Marines.

69
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:50,552
So I'll become a pirate.

70
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,137
That I can promise you.

71
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:54,017
But I want you to know one thing.

72
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:58,677
While I'm with you, the only thing I
dedicate myself to is fulfilling my ambition.

73
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,590
Which is?

74
00:03:59,673 --> 00:04:02,875
To be nothing less than the
world's greatest swordsman.

75
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:05,497
If somewhere along the way
I have to give that up,

76
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,757
then I want you to accept responsibility.

77
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:10,260
After which, you get to apologize to me.

78
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,460
The world's greatest swordsman.

79
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:13,938
Sounds pretty good.

80
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:18,437
The King of the Pirates wouldn't have
any less than the best on his crew.

81
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,480
Big talker.

82
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:22,677
From this point on, no matter
if I'm a criminal or not,

83
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:25,701
I will spread the name
Zoro throughout the world.

84
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:27,837
What are you standing there frozen for?

85
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,685
I want you to kill all
three of them right now!

86
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,000
You might want to duck!

87
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,760
Gum-Gum!

88
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,310
Yes!

89
00:04:41,393 --> 00:04:42,720
You knocked them all down!

90
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,808
Wanna tell me what you are?

91
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,680
I'm just a guy who ate the Gum-Gum fruit.

92
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,600
What's the Gum-Gum fruit?

93
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,741
A rubber person?

94
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:53,917
It looks like he does have
the Devil Fruit powers.

95
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,017
Captain, we don't stand
a chance against them.

96
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:57,117
Yeah, just look at them!

97
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,037
They're insane!

98
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,591
We couldn't even take on Zoro by himself!

99
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:04,057
This is a direct order.

100
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:08,057
Every marine that just spouted weakness,
pull your gun out and shoot yourself.

101
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:14,917
I can't do anything with
weak soldiers but babies.

102
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,840
This will be easy.

103
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,520
Rankless lowlife bums!

104
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:36,400
You have no right to defy my superiority!

105
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:38,920
I am Marine Captain X-Hand Morgan!

106
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,740
And I'm Luffy!

107
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,280
Nice to meet ya!

108
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:56,400
Look! He's been hit!

109
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,760
You're right!

110
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,060
Now die!

111
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:04,320
I don't think so!

112
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:09,093
The captain's getting bubbled out there.

113
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,580
It's embarrassing.

114
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:18,400
Call yourself a marine, but you
destroyed my friend Kobe's dream!

115
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:20,960
Straw Hat!

116
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,097
Stop right there!

117
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,298
Look at what I got!

118
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:26,180
Are you stupid or something?

119
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:27,290
I said stop!

120
00:06:27,373 --> 00:06:31,217
If you would pay attention to me, I have
a hostage here you might want to look at!

121
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,241
Helmepo's crazy!

122
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:33,610
Hey.

123
00:06:33,693 --> 00:06:34,523
Huh?

124
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,637
If you value your Squad little
friend's life, you won't move a muscle!

125
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,550
I'm serious!

126
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:41,736
Why move and I'll shoot him, I swear!

127
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:46,742
Wolf, listen!

128
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,017
Don't let anything that happens
to me stop you no matter what!

129
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,080
Even if I die!

130
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,620
Of course, you got it!

131
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,737
You hear that, you big idiot?

132
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:57,420
Koby is ready to die by your hand.

133
00:06:58,580 --> 00:06:59,680
Don't you move!

134
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,557
I said don't move or I'll shoot!

135
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:02,470
I swear it!

136
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,470
Luffy!

137
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:05,660
Gum-Gum!

138
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,140
Time's up!

139
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:10,840
For I am Fearless Marine
Captain Axe and Morgan!

140
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,316
Daddy, hurry up and kill him already!

141
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,310
Hey, stop!

142
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,020
Nice one!

143
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:31,300
Thank you.

144
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:33,980
I'm just doing my job, Captain.

145
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:43,604
Captain Morgas has been beaten!

146
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,590
Unbelievable!

147
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,094
Those guys are unreal!

148
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:51,749
If there's anyone else who wants to step
forward to fight us, then do it now.

149
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,640
We're free!

150
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:58,150
Finally!

151
00:07:58,233 --> 00:07:59,800
The train is over!

152
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,020
Such a glorious day!

153
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,580
That's weird.

154
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:06,577
Looks like they're all happy
that their captain was beaten.

155
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:10,778
They must have been afraid of him
for a long time before we showed up!

156
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:16,700
Zoro! Are you okay? What's wrong?

157
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:19,660
I'm just... hungry.

158
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:26,120
I am stuffed!

159
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:31,947
Having not eaten for three weeks, I was
ready to gnaw up through my bootstraps!

160
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:38,527
I can't believe you're
finished, Lightweight.

161
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:42,377
How the hell can you have a bigger appetite
than a guy who hasn't eaten in weeks?

162
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,157
It just tastes too good, I guess.

163
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,070
Right, Colby?

164
00:08:45,153 --> 00:08:46,020
Yeah, it's great.

165
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,720
Thanks for fixing it for us. My pleasure.

166
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,297
After all, you guys did save the town.

167
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:53,817
You're the most amazing man I've ever met!

168
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,380
Yeah, I am, I know.

169
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:59,972
I'll be more amazing when I'm king of
the pirates and I have the One Piece.

170
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:02,060
Oh, and the best crew on the seas.

171
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:06,557
Luffy, where are you and your crew
planning on traveling when you leave here?

172
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:07,897
You mean it's not obvious?

173
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:10,392
We're headed straight for the Grand Line!

174
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,250
No!

175
00:09:12,333 --> 00:09:13,437
Have you completely lost your mind?

176
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,517
You have two crew members!

177
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,817
There's no way you're equipped
ahead of the Grand Line, Luffy!

178
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:19,937
I've heard about it, but I never
knew it was such an awful place.

179
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:21,640
It's worse than you think!

180
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:24,817
You know that this world
has two oceans, I'm sure.

181
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:28,277
There is an enormous land mass
that cuts across both of them.

182
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,020
This is called the Red Line.

183
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:34,417
Legend tells of a town that sits
dead center on the Red Line.

184
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:37,597
The Grand Line is set to cut
through this town at a right

185
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:41,151
angle and stretch all the way
around the rest of the world.

186
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,900
The story goes on to say that Gold Roger,

187
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:49,728
the King of the Pirates, had once obtained
everything this world had to offer.

188
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:54,962
Before he died, he said that he left the
great One Piece treasure at this location.

189
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:58,840
Ever since, pirates have
set sail for the Grand Line.

190
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,330
Today,

191
00:10:00,413 --> 00:10:05,400
the place is nothing but a battlefield,
and some even call it the Pirate Graveyard.

192
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:11,497
I heard stories about it
from people passing through.

193
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:13,557
The customers say that no
one who has ever entered

194
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,677
the Grand Line comes
out of that place alive.

195
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:19,097
Which is really too bad, because that's
where the One Piece is said to be?

196
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,337
and that's exactly where we're going.

197
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,660
I guess we have to live with it. No!

198
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:24,921
You can't agree!

199
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,010
What do you care?

200
00:10:26,093 --> 00:10:26,937
You're not going with us, are you?

201
00:10:27,020 --> 00:10:28,420
No, but I still worry.

202
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:31,328
Is it so wrong to care
about the two of you?

203
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:34,517
Luffy and I haven't known each
other for years or anything,

204
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,357
but I'd still consider him a friend.

205
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,440
Wouldn't you say? Of course!

206
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:41,816
We may have to part ways,
but we'll always be friends.

207
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:48,920
When I was just a little
kid, I never had any friends,

208
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:52,534
much less anyone who would
bother fighting on my behalf.

209
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:56,333
So I always tried my hardest
never to fight for anything.

210
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:01,677
But the two of you have taught me a
lesson I could never learn on my own,

211
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:03,637
how to live for what I believe in!

212
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:07,057
So I've decided to make my
one childhood dream a reality,

213
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,757
and I'm going to join the Marines!

214
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:13,487
Then don't you think you should be a
little more concerned with your situation?

215
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:17,217
I mean, you did spend two
years in Alvita's pirate ship,

216
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:19,829
even if you were nothing
but her cabin boy.

217
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:24,317
The Marines' information
gathering is top-notch.

218
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:27,697
They'll find out about your time
with Alvida, and you'll never join.

219
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:29,240
I never thought of that.

220
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,060
Hey, you there!

221
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:38,217
We heard that you fellas
are actually pirates.

222
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:39,418
Is this rumor true?

223
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:41,737
Right, and I just added the
first member to my crew.

224
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:44,497
So pretty much the whole
thing just became official.

225
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:47,057
We appreciate everything you
did to save our town from

226
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:50,297
that horrible tyrant who
terrorized us all for so long.

227
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:51,210
However,

228
00:11:51,293 --> 00:11:52,337
now that we know that you're pirates,

229
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:55,891
we cannot sit idly by and watch
you go about your business.

230
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:59,237
Therefore, you and your crew will
need to leave this town immediately.

231
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:03,377
But out of respect for what you've done,
we will not report you to headquarters.

232
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:04,500
Are you crazy?

233
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:06,617
How do you find the
nerve to talk like that?

234
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:10,417
Before these pirates came along, you
guys were as scared of Borgen as we were.

235
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:12,697
Without them, we'd still
be under his reign.

236
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,074
We owe them our lives.

237
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:19,840
Well, time to go.

238
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,357
Thanks for all of the food, lady.

239
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,517
Hey, wait a second.

240
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,953
You're leaving already?

241
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,090
Yeah.

242
00:12:33,180 --> 00:12:35,460
Aren't you part of the crew as well?

243
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:37,820
Well, I...

244
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:43,980
Hold it.

245
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:45,740
Is he with you or what?

246
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:50,582
What I can tell you is what he's
been busy doing up to this point.

247
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:52,480
Mulfi, you wouldn't!

248
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:56,320
Yeah, there was this
fantastically fat pirate lady.

249
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,127
I think her name was Alvida.

250
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,190
Mofi!

251
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:04,160
If they find out I ran with the pirate
crew, I'll never join the marine.

252
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:08,020
She carried around this
huge iron club, and boy,

253
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,677
she was the nastiest looking
woman I've ever seen.

254
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:15,540
For two years, this wimpy kid was her
own private cabin boy. Please stop.

255
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,280
You can't do this.

256
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:18,500
Mofi, no!

257
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,470
No!

258
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,920
Now that was a dumb move!

259
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,430
Bastard!

260
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,440
Get out of here now!

261
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:40,037
We can't have you pirates ripping up
this town any more than you already have,

262
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:40,950
you hear me?

263
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:42,210
Enough.

264
00:13:42,293 --> 00:13:43,123
You made your point.

265
00:13:43,206 --> 00:13:44,884
Now let him fall to the ground.

266
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:51,297
It's obvious you're not Gourmet?

267
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:52,677
So stop badgering the poor kid!

268
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,407
and take your leave of
our town this instant!

269
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,960
That was on purpose?

270
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:06,000
Luffy did that just to help me out.

271
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:12,457
He worked me up and got me so mad that I'd

272
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:15,069
hit him and look like
I wasn't on his side.

273
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:22,302
Even at the very end of our journey together,
I wound up continuing to rely on him.

274
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,700
I couldn't do anything for myself.

275
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,182
Nothing's changed for me at all.

276
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,640
I am such an idiot!

277
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:34,810
Sir!

278
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:37,100
Please, sir! Please,

279
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:39,217
you have to let me join
the Marines I'll clean

280
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:42,037
and scrub and do any chores
that you'd like me to.

281
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,238
I'll do anything to become a Marine!

282
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:50,465
Lieutenant, I can't say
I fully trust this kid?

283
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:53,337
I wouldn't be against the
idea if there weren't clear

284
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:56,538
cases of certain Marines
actually being pirate spies.

285
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:00,202
I say we should conduct
a background check first.

286
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:03,949
No matter what you say, I am a
man who will become a Marine!

287
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:07,950
Hmm.

288
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:12,497
I can't tell you how many of our comrades

289
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:14,957
have been killed by
pirates over the years.

290
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,780
This is a big step you're taking. So?

291
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,708
Permission to join granted.

292
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:22,990
Sir!

293
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:26,677
That was a thin act you put on back there.

294
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,077
I wouldn't be surprised if
they see right through it.

295
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:31,237
Kobe should be able to
handle the rest on his own.

296
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,277
I have faith in him.

297
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:34,197
It is a fitting way to leave this place.

298
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:36,957
Unable to turn back because
everyone here hates us now.

299
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:38,160
Very pirate-like.

300
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,820
Yeah, it sure is. Buffy!

301
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,160
I can never thank you enough!

302
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,617
You've done more for me
than anyone ever has!

303
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:51,876
I've never heard of a marine
thanking a pirate before.

304
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:54,041
That's one for the history books.

305
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:59,760
We'll meet again, Kobe!
Someday! Bye, Luffy.

306
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:01,785
Hope to see you again someday!

307
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,020
All hands salute!

308
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,020
See ya!

309
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,678
That's a good friend you have there.

310
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:20,650
Men,

311
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:24,271
seeing as our current salute
is in violation of marine law,

312
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:26,949
we will all go without
food for three days.

313
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,300
Do we all understand this?

314
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:30,560
Yes, sir!

315
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,540
Now, let's go!

316
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:40,100
It's time for us to set our
heading for the Grand Line!

317
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:55,777
As a kid, I never stopped.

318
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:58,357
Searching for a great treasure!

319
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:03,137
I had a map in my mind.

320
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:05,757
That I knew would lead me.

321
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:09,957
I had to find my way to that place!

322
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,880
Before someone could beat me.

323
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:17,037
The promised land was in my grasp.

324
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,580
And I wouldn't let go!

325
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:23,497
La la la la?

326
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:24,937
My only dream.

327
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:27,100
La la la la la!

328
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:32,920
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true!

329
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:38,257
But if the world ever changes,

330
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:41,737
I call out your name!

331
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:48,337
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

332
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:55,257
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade!

333
00:17:55,340 --> 00:18:00,380
Waiting for that one true dream?
